-- title:
--   Gauss centre of the j-finite chart of X₁(M) is (varpi)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M\ge 5$ an integer with $p\nmid M$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and $\zeta\in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$ in $L$, and let $\varpi\in A$ generate the maximal ideal. Let $K_M$ be the intermediate field of $L\subseteq L((q))$ generated over $L$ by the image, under coefficientwise application of $\mathbb{Q}\to L$, of the $q$-expansion field of $X_1(M)$ (the $\Gamma_1(M)$ field inside $\mathbb{Q}((q))$), viewed as an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A\subseteq L\subseteq K_M$. Let $j_M\in K_M$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion $q^{-1}$ times the rational $j$-numerator power series, i.e. the $q$-expansion of $j$. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K_M$ whose elements are exactly those $f$ admitting $x,y\in A[[q]]$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ and $f\cdot y=x$ in $L((q))$. Then for every element $s$ of the ring of elements of $K_M$ integral over $A[j_M]$, if $s$ is a nonunit of $W_0$ (i.e. lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$), then $s$ lies in the ideal generated by $\varpi$ in that ring.
--
--   This identifies the centre of the Gauss valuation on the $j$-finite chart ring of $X_1(M)$ at a level $M$ prime to $p$: the contraction of the maximal ideal of the Gauss valuation ring to the integral closure of $A[j]$ in the $q$-expansion field is contained in, hence equal to, $(\varpi)$. It is the step used to show that the localisation of this chart ring at the Gauss prime is a discrete valuation ring with the expected fraction field.
